WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:01.935
Want to turn now to some last

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:02.569
minute drama

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:04.237
in the Fox News defamation case.

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:06.072
That trial was supposed to start today,

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:07.540
but it has been delayed.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.175
And CNN watched as lawyers

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:09.642
for Dominion

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.845
voting systems brought more than 40 boxes

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:13.046
into the courthouse today,

00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:15.181
most likely evidence and other materials.

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.716
CNN's Oliver Dorsey joins us now.

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:17.717
He's outside the courthouse

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:19.085
in Wilmington, Delaware.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:21.254
Oliver, what is happening

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:24.557
some 11th hour,

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:25.492
11th hour twist

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:27.027
really casting in a question

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.561
of whether a trial, John,

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.363
is even going to take place.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:31.865
Right behind me,

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:33.733
was where it's supposed to have started.

00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:34.434
Opening arguments

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:35.668
were supposed to be taking place

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.070
right about now.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.439
But last night, the judge abruptly

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:40.540
delayed the trial, saying

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.509
it's going to now start on Tuesday.

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:43.610
And there's no reason

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:44.711
given the judge said today

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:45.445
that he doesn't find it

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:46.246
unusual for this

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:48.681
to have been delayed by one day.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:50.116
But Rupert Murdoch's

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:50.550
Wall Street

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.851
Journal as well, as some other outlets

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:53.720
now reporting that

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:54.487
a last minute

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.022
settlement might be in the works,

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:57.157
that Fox might be pushing

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:58.224
to settle this case,

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:59.492
avert a trial

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:00.760
and really spare

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:01.895
some of its high profile

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:04.330
talent and executives like Rupert Murdoch

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.832
from having to take the stand

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:06.633
and testify

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:07.934
as to why they allowed

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:11.004
election lies to be broadcast on Fox,

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:13.873
despite knowing that they were not true.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.776
Now, both sides are still preparing

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:17.644
for a trial.

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:18.178
The judge said

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:19.679
basically to be back tomorrow

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:20.480
and a trial will start

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.248
if a settlement is not reached.

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:23.216
Dominion

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:24.751
brought in about 40 boxes

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.953
earlier of evidence into the courtroom.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.621
So they're clearly ready, John,

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:29.823
to go to trial.

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:31.591
If a settlement is not reached.

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.926
Right now, everything

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:35.061
sort of seems just up in the air,

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:36.129
up in the air.

00:01:36.129 --> 00:01:37.430
We'll see how the negotiations

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.364
go behind closed doors.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:39.199
Oliver, keep us posted.

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:40.133
If anything, changes.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.701
Let's bring in our senior legal analyst,

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.036
Ellie Hoenig.

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:43.770
Good morning.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.039
There's so much on the table here. Twist.

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:47.874
I know the plot thickens.

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:48.808
What a twist.

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:49.976
Why would a judge do this?

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:52.278
Well, so if you go to a judge in either

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:53.746
a criminal or civil case

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:54.547
on the eve of trial

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.950
and say we're making close progressions

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:57.884
towards a settlement

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:58.985
or in a criminal case,

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.120
this is not a criminal case

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.287
towards a guilty plea.

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:03.156
Often judges will say, okay,

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:03.990
I'll give you a day,

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:04.757
I'll give you two days,

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:05.792
maybe I'll give you a week.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:07.260
I'll give you a chance to work it out.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.329
I think that's the most likely scenario

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.131
we've seen reporting consistent

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:11.798
with that as well.

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:12.532
So you think there's

00:02:12.532 --> 00:02:13.700
you think there's probably

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.135
those hawks somewhere going,

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.002
yeah, there's something about

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.303
being on the eve of trial

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:19.572
that can really sober up both parties.

00:02:19.572 --> 00:02:20.640
It's a reality, right?

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:21.307
Look, look at it.

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:22.542
From Fox's point of view,

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:23.476
they're looking

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:24.844
at the likelihood,

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:25.945
if there's a trial

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:27.147
of having all of

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:28.281
there are many of their

00:02:28.281 --> 00:02:29.582
most prominent anchors

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.551
have to take the stand, testify

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:32.585
and get cross-examined.

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:33.520
So and the owners

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.722
and the top executive executives,

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:36.322
they're up to

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:37.657
and including Rupert Murdoch.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:39.259
And so you can understand why

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:40.193
they would be hit

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:41.561
by reality at the last moment,

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:43.463
say we need to avoid this.

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:43.963
And, you know,

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:44.664
another question is,

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:46.533
why would Dominion be interested

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:47.734
in potentially settling this?

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.102
Because as we've discussed,

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:50.670
I think Dominion has a very

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.772
strong case here for defamation.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:53.940
But the fact of the matter is,

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.009
nothing's sure when it comes to a jury.

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:56.976
There's always risk

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:58.478
when it comes to a jury trial.

00:02:58.478 --> 00:03:00.146
Juries, just 12 human beings,

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:01.981
you never know what they're going to do.

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:04.217
So if if there is a settlement.

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:05.552
Help us understand,

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:06.452
because it's beyond

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:07.720
how much money they settle for

00:03:07.720 --> 00:03:08.254
which I think

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:10.423
gets a disproportionate amount

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:11.791
of attention.

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:12.992
But how much is a lot of do

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.761
I and I understand that.

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:16.429
I think also the company

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:17.397
has a lot of money.

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:18.932
What I think is fascinating,

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:19.966
if there is a settlement,

00:03:19.966 --> 00:03:20.500
is does it

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.368
come with an admission of guilt,

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:23.836
an apology? Right.

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.471
Or an admission of wrongdoing?

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.406
So there's a couple of things

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:27.740
that are in play here

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:28.875
if there's a negotiation.

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:29.642
First of all, of course,

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:30.677
there's the amount parties

00:03:30.677 --> 00:03:32.011
will go back and forth on that.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:32.845
Second of all, there's

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:34.380
will this be confidential?

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.082
Usually settlements like this

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:36.849
are confidential.

00:03:36.849 --> 00:03:37.817
We don't know the numbers

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:39.686
unless we get it through reporting,

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:41.054
but we wouldn't know it officially.

00:03:41.054 --> 00:03:42.589
But the parties are free to negotiate.

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:43.323
This number will

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:45.124
or will not be confidential.

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:46.459
And then the parties can negotiate

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:47.126
for any sort

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:48.528
of admission of guilt,

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:50.163
statement, acknowledgment,

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:51.364
retraction, etc.

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:52.465
But keep in mind,

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:54.534
the judge here has already made a finding

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:56.035
as a matter of law

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:57.270
that Fox his statements

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.438
about the 2020 election

00:03:58.438 --> 00:04:00.273
and about Dominion were false.

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:02.275
So that is on the record.

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:02.875
The only question

00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:03.710
that trial was going to be

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:05.478
Is there actual malice?

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:06.613
Did Fox know

00:04:06.613 --> 00:04:08.581
or were they reckless about the falsity?

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.782
So no matter what

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.818
Dominion has that finding a falsity.

00:04:11.818 --> 00:04:12.151
Okay.

00:04:12.151 --> 00:04:13.987
So then 1.6 million, you're right.

00:04:13.987 --> 00:04:15.388
It's a lot of money for the foxes

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:16.256
deep pockets, right?

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:16.456
Yes.

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:17.290
And their viewers

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.759
will probably not believe

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:21.060
that they did anything wrong,

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:21.995
that they were targeted, you know.

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:23.429
So I'm not sure what it does

00:04:23.429 --> 00:04:24.530
to their credibility.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:24.697
Right.

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:27.133
Because it's kind of, you know, well,

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:28.234
the facts are out there, right?

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:29.235
We've all seen the text.

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:29.836
They're all out there

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:31.004
and we have the funding from the judge.

00:04:31.004 --> 00:04:31.170
Okay.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.538
So the $1.6 billion,

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:33.906
